  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Utah Code 53-5-704): (1) (a) Except as provided in Subsection (1)(b), the bureau shall issue a permit to carry a concealed firearm for lawful self defense to an applicant who is 21 years of age or older within 60 days after receiving an application, unless the bureau finds proof that the applicant does not meet the qualifications described in Subsection (2).\nSection 1 (Utah Code 53-5-704): (b) (i) Within 90 days before the day on which a provisional permit holder under Section 53-5-704.5 reaches 21 years of age, the provisional permit holder may apply under this section for a permit to carry a concealed firearm for lawful self defense.\nSection 1 (Utah Code 53-5-704): (ii) The bureau shall issue a permit to an applicant under Subsection (1)(b)(i) within 60 days after receiving an application, unless the bureau finds proof that the applicant does not meet the qualifications described in Subsection (2).\nSection 1 (Utah Code 53-5-704): (iii) A permit issued under this Subsection (1)(b) is not valid until an applicant reaches 21 years of age."
